1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,140
One letter left.

2
00:00:01,140 --> 00:00:01,700
I'm Mara.

3
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:04,430
My mother is on the
other side of this wall.

4
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:07,693
I could write any
word, except that one.

5
00:00:07,903 --> 00:00:09,263
Help was always to me.

6
00:00:09,263 --> 00:00:11,053
And I always came alone.

7
00:00:11,253 --> 00:00:13,833
So I bent my last
tube into one letter.

8
00:00:14,433 --> 00:00:16,833
And through the wall,
my mother bent hers.

9
00:00:17,423 --> 00:00:18,293
Us.

10
00:00:19,193 --> 00:00:20,903
And the whole street answered.

11
00:00:22,203 --> 00:00:24,563
Stop that! You'll
break the ring!

12
00:00:24,563 --> 00:00:26,683
Sir, I'm going to have
to ask you to leave.

13
00:00:26,883 --> 00:00:30,083
Fool! Break the ring,
and they all go out!

14
00:00:30,183 --> 00:00:32,183
Out. Yes. That's the idea.

15
00:00:33,383 --> 00:00:34,623
And out they came.

16
00:00:34,623 --> 00:00:34,973
Ruth.

17
00:00:34,973 --> 00:00:35,323
Otis.

18
00:00:35,323 --> 00:00:37,973
Pete, still asking
about his oven.

19
00:00:38,363 --> 00:00:39,873
The other me took my hand.

20
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:41,753
And then there was just me.

21
00:00:42,953 --> 00:00:44,283
Mara?

22
00:00:44,583 --> 00:00:45,553
Mom.

23
00:00:46,163 --> 00:00:47,953
Look how tall you are.

24
00:00:48,043 --> 00:00:49,483
You left your coat.

25
00:00:50,183 --> 00:00:52,323
I'm not crying.
I'm leaking argon.

26
00:00:52,833 --> 00:00:56,163
By morning, every light on
the street was just a light.

27
00:00:56,463 --> 00:00:56,713
Mara?

28
00:00:56,713 --> 00:00:58,583
When did we get a number eleven?

29
00:00:58,983 --> 00:01:00,483
And somebody knocked.
